{"t":1378481.7984409,"req":"h07","event":"done","status":"answered","level":0,"steps":["classify","retrieve","draft"],"answer":"Moshi\u2019s Inner Monologue is a hierarchical, multi\u2011stream architecture that first generates a sequence of text tokens (the \u201cinner monologue\u201d) and then uses those tokens as a prefix to predict aligned semantic and acoustic tokens for speech. This decomposition allows the model to produce both text and audio in a single generative process, enabling real\u2011time, full\u2011duplex speech\u2011to\u2011speech dialogue while preserving paralinguistic information and allowing streaming TTS/ASR by adjusting the delay between token types. [C:moshi:7]"}
